meta {
  name: Create job - oversized body
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/jobs
  body: json
  auth: none
}

script:pre-request {
  // Build a >50 KB body at send time so no large literal is committed to the
  // repo. 60000 chars keeps the body comfortably over MAX_BODY_BYTES (51200).
  bru.setVar("oversizedDescription", "x".repeat(60000));
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Oversized",
    "company": "Acme Corp",
    "description": "{{oversizedDescription}}"
  }
}

docs {
  The BodySizeLimitMiddleware rejects any request body over 50 KB
  (MAX_BODY_BYTES = 51200 bytes) before it is parsed, counting the actual bytes
  streamed rather than trusting Content-Length.

  To trip the guard without committing a large literal to the repo, the
  pre-request script generates a 60000-char string at send time and stores it in
  the runtime var `oversizedDescription`, which the body references via
  `{{oversizedDescription}}`. Just send the request as-is.

  Expected (body > 50 KB): 422 Unprocessable Entity
  Body: Pydantic-shaped envelope, detail[0].type = "too_large".

  This case is also covered by the automated pytest suite
  (tests/test_body_limit.py), including the streamed-in-chunks and
  lying-Content-Length variants.
}
